# Global gitignore, installed as ~/.config/git/ignore.
#
# Git reads that path on every platform with no config entry pointing at it,
# which is why this is a link rather than a core.excludesFile setting.
#
# The bar for a line here: it is noise produced by an operating system, an
# editor, or a tool, on any repository you happen to open. Anything specific to
# one project belongs in that project's .gitignore, where the rest of the team
# can see it. Ignoring a project's build output globally is how a build output
# directory ends up missing from a clone for everyone else.

# ---------- macOS ----------
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# ---------- Windows ----------
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# ---------- Linux ----------
.directory
.Trash-*
.nfs*

# ---------- Editors ----------
# Only the per-user state. A project's committed .vscode/extensions.json or
# .idea run configuration is deliberate and shared, so neither directory is
# ignored wholesale here.
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.*.swp
.*.swo
.vscode/settings.json
.idea/workspace.xml
.idea/tasks.xml

# ---------- Tools ----------
# Local environment overrides that should never be committed anywhere.
*.local
!*.local.example
.env.local
